#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138526 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0576504-7bd6-5649-99fe-a758faaffa4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations Containing Single-Digit Decimals"}] :question/id #uuid "6ff19222-3f56-53cf-bd39-b399573664b8" :question/math-academy-id "e-13026" :question/problem "What is the solution to the equation $0.9s=3.6$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.9s &= 3.6 \\\\\n10 \\cdot (0.9s) &= 10 \\cdot (3.6) \\\\\n9s &= 36\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9s &= 36 \\\\\n\\frac{9s}{9} &= \\frac{36}{9} \\\\\n\\frac{9s}{9} &= \\frac{36}{9} \\\\\ns &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138078 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138527 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "039fc0a8-337f-50b3-be2c-cfbdbd399537" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations Containing Two-Digit Decimals"}] :question/id #uuid "015eac36-e18d-5a53-bfff-f301722a1f0c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13027" :question/problem "What is the solution to the equation $0.25s=0.5$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.25s &= 0.5 \\\\\n100 \\cdot (0.25s) &= 100 \\cdot (0.5) \\\\\n25s &= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25s &= 50 \\\\\n\\frac{25s}{25} &= \\frac{50}{25} \\\\\n\\frac{25s}{25} &= \\frac{50}{25} \\\\\ns &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138079 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138528 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68f57411-1d39-52cd-86ee-abf633adf3c3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "49ed1c21-223b-5dda-8f4d-7b6a3492a26b" :question/math-academy-id "e-13028" :question/problem "If $0.25+0.03z=1$, then what is the value of $z$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.25 + 0.03z &= 1 \\\\\n100 \\cdot (0.25 + 0.03z) &= 100 \\cdot (1) \\\\\n100 \\cdot (0.25) + 100 \\cdot (0.03z) &= 100 \\\\\n25 + 3z &= 100\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25 + 3z &= 100 \\\\\n3z + 25 &= 100 \\\\\n3z + 25 - 25 &= 100 - 25 \\\\\n3z &= 75 \\\\\n\\frac{3z}{3} &= \\frac{75}{3} \\\\\nz &= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
